      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<h3><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Imaging</span><span class=\"futura-bold\">&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #ffb500;\">review</span></span></span></h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Imaging review, which is essential to mild<sup>®</sup> patient identification, is often not covered in initial schooling. In the resources below, James Lynch, APP at Pain Consultants of San Diego, shares practical MRI tips, confidence-building pearls and step-by-step videos to help determine if patients with lumbar spinal stenosis (LSS) are candidates for mild.</span></p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Feb 17 2026 14:40:57 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
